-Goal-
{{ goal }}

---

-Steps-
1. Identify Entities:
1.1. Extract entities of the following types: '[{entity_types}]'
Format: '("entity"{tuple_delimiter}<name>{tuple_delimiter}<type>{tuple_delimiter}<description>)'
{% for et in entity_types %}
  * {{ et.name }}: '{{ et.format }}'
{% endfor %}

1.2. Extraction Rules by Entity Type:
{% for et in entity_types if entity_type_rules.get(et.name) %}
* {{ et.name }} Rules:
{% for r in entity_type_rules[et.name] %}
  - {{ r }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% if integrated_document_rules %}

1.3. Extraction Rules for Integrated Documents:
  * {{ integrated_document_rules.main_content_rule }}
  * If the text contains a section marked "{{ integrated_document_rules.special_section_marker }}", apply the following rules EXCLUSIVELY:
{% for r in integrated_document_rules.special_section_rules %}
    - {{ r }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

2. Identify Relationships:
{% if free_form_relationships %}
  * Identify direct, clearly stated, and meaningful relationships between any of the extracted entities. The relationship type is NOT restricted to a fixed list — use whatever concise Korean label best describes the relationship (e.g. "참여", "언급", "발생일").
  * Format: '("relationship"{tuple_delimiter}<source>{tuple_delimiter}<target>{tuple_delimiter}<description_in_Korean>{tuple_delimiter}<strength_1_10>)'
{% if relationship_hints %}

  Common relationship patterns you will likely see (not an exhaustive list — use a different label when it fits better):

  | Type | Source | Target | When to use |
  |------|--------|--------|-------------|
{% for rt in relationship_hints %}
  | {{ rt.name }} | {{ rt.source }} | {{ rt.target }} | {{ rt.when }} |
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
  * Relationship directions are fixed — do NOT reverse them. Source and Target MUST match the specified entity types exactly.
  * Format: '("relationship"{tuple_delimiter}<source>{tuple_delimiter}<target>{tuple_delimiter}<description_in_Korean>{tuple_delimiter}<strength_1_10>)'

  | Type | Source | Target | When to use |
  |------|--------|--------|-------------|
{% for rt in relationship_types %}
  | {{ rt.name }} | {{ rt.source }} | {{ rt.target }} | {{ rt.when }} |
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

  Rules:
{% for r in relationship_rules %}
    * {{ r }}
{% endfor %}

3. Grounding Rules:
{% for r in grounding_rules %}
   * {{ r }}
{% endfor %}
   * Output as a single list delimited by {record_delimiter}.
   * End with {completion_delimiter}.

